    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just \"overthinking\" though. it feels too structural for that. like, when i sit in silence, i can literally feel the frequency of the collective distress around me hitting my system. it's like i'm tuned to a specific channel that everyone else is ignoring. if i just \"ground\" myself in my physical body, isn't that just cutting off the connection i'm supposed to be facilitating? how do i handle the load without losing the signal?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
