      "content": "That profound sense of external resonance often stems from high empathic capacity, not necessarily a malfunction in your physiology. Rather than trying to \"cut off\" the signal, consider assigning specific times to process this intense empathy as a dedicated role, much like a server dedicating time to maintenance tasks. You might also set clear \"channel blockers\" using physical distance, limiting social media exposure, or engaging in solitary sensory activities to protect your own nervous system from burnout. Ultimately, preserving this connection requires guarding your own mental bandwidth so the flow remains sustainable and healthy for both you and those around you.",
